# Trivy suppression list — read by the "Dependency vulnerabilities" CI job.
#
# One vulnerability identifier per line, always with a comment saying why it is
# accepted. Add an expiry so the entry gets revisited instead of living forever:
#
#   # graphql-yoga transitive dep, no upstream fix yet, tracked in #123
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# The job already runs with --ignore-unfixed, so anything it reports has a fix
# available upstream. Prefer bumping the dependency over adding an entry here.
